The fix for crbug 578676178 (restricted: "[ServiceWorker] Check
NavigationPreloadRequest lifetime in callbacks"): chromium/src main commit
c6cefaec9eb730ff6b74251e36d56f35cd7e3c10 (main@{#1745182}), merged to the 159
branch as 4223761c8254a6ba8adc8ed9485366e499d52ef3. Its 158 merge (Gerrit
8825921) is pending, as of 8127@{#1837}.

NavigationPreloadRequest::OnReceiveRedirect() and OnComplete() resolve the
navigation preload response promise before telling the context client the
preload completed. Resolving the promise can run the service worker's script
synchronously, which may destroy the worker context and with it the request
object still on the stack: a use-after-free in the renderer, reachable from a
page's service worker.

This is the main commit's change without its tests (the new
service_worker_context_client_unittest.cc, web_embedded_worker_impl_test.cc
and content/test/BUILD.gn). 158's files are the same as the main commit's
parent, so the result is byte-identical to main's and to 159's merge. Drop
this once 158 gets the fix (check that the merged change is the same).

